# BISECT STEP 3 — KernelSU core only.  DIAGNOSTIC ONLY, DO NOT SHIP.
#
# Where the bisection stands:
#   step 1 (bisect-nosusfs): KSU on,  NoMount on,  SuSFS off -> CRASHES
#   step 2 (bisect-noksu):   KSU off, NoMount off, SuSFS off -> NO CRASH
# so the cause is KernelSU core or NoMount, and the base LineageOS 4.9.337 kernel
# plus our non-root patches are exonerated (as is the whole SuSFS backport).
#
# This step keeps KernelSU and drops NoMount:
#   crash still happens -> KernelSU core. Next split is KSU's runtime sepolicy
#                          rule application (the policydb surgery: add_type/
#                          apply_kernelsu_rules under policy_rwlock).
#   crash goes away     -> NoMount is the cause, and the NoMount VFS-redirect
#                          engine gets the next audit.
#
# Build with:  BISECT=1 EXTRA_FRAGMENT=bisect-ksuonly.fragment \
#              ./scripts/build.sh --profile=release
CONFIG_KSU=y
CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK=y
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_PATH is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MOUNT is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_KSTAT is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_UNAME is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_CMDLINE_OR_BOOTCONFIG is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_OPEN_REDIRECT is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG is not set
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_HIDE_KSU_SUSFS_SYMBOLS is not set
# CONFIG_NOMOUNT is not set
